@Animations
You can define up to four animations which can then be used in element
definitions. These animations are usually time-based but sometimes they
might not be; they can also be based on coordinates.

The "Animation edit" field selects which of the four animations you
want to edit, numbered from 0 to 3.

You can set the amount to add to the appearance mapping offsets defined
in the element definitions for each of four steps of the animation. These
additions are always modulo 128. The step number is usually time-based,
but sometimes the coordinates also affect which step to use.

X1, X2, Y1, and Y2 define the pattern for considering the coordinates of
tiles to decide the animation step differently for each tiles; if none
of them are selected then the animation step is the same for the entire
board grid at a specific time. SLOW will make time-based animations slower,
taking two frames per step; if not selected then one frame per step.

At the bottom is the preview display of the animation; for time 0 on the
left and time 3 on the right. This will show the patterns which are
controlled by the parameters above, so that you can see how they are
desired. Use the "Preview from" field to set which appearance mapping
offset to add to the numbers given in the step fields for the preview;
the "Preview from" field will not be saved in the world file.

See also:
!-appmap;Appearance mapping

